  "frontmatter": {
    "title": "Callouts And Code In MDX",
    "description": "Use callouts, GitHub alerts, and code fence titles, line highlights, and diffs in MDX pages."
  },
  "content": "<h1>Callouts And Code In MDX</h1>\n<p><code>.mdx</code> pages support the same callout and code fence syntax as\n<a href=\"/docs/developer-guides/callouts-and-code\">Markdown pages</a>. They are compiled\nto sanitized static HTML at build time.</p>\n<h2>Callouts</h2>\n<p>Write <code>:::type Title</code> on the first line and <code>:::</code> on the last line. The five\ntypes are <code>note</code>, <code>tip</code>, <code>info</code>, <code>warning</code>, and <code>danger</code>. In MDX, use a\nplain-text title.</p>\n<div class=\"admonition admonition-note\" role=\"note\" aria-label=\"Note\"><p class=\"admonition-title\">Note</p><div class=\"admonition-content\"><p>MDX callouts hold <strong>Markdown</strong> and code.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"admonition admonition-warning\" role=\"note\" aria-label=\"Breaking change\"><p class=\"admonition-title\">Breaking change</p><div class=\"admonition-content\"><p><code>generate:docs</code> now validates frontmatter.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"admonition admonition-info\" role=\"note\" aria-label=\"Outer\"><p class=\"admonition-title\">Outer</p><div class=\"admonition-content\"><p>Give the outer fence more colons to nest callouts.</p><div class=\"admonition admonition-tip\" role=\"note\" aria-label=\"Inner\"><p class=\"admonition-title\">Inner</p><div class=\"admonition-content\"><p>Inner callout.</p></div></div></div></div>\n<p><code>:::details Title</code> makes a collapsible callout that starts closed.</p>\n<details class=\"admonition admonition-details\"><summary class=\"admonition-title\">Show more</summary><div class=\"admonition-content\"><p>Collapsible callouts work in MDX too.</p></div></details>\n<p>The <code>&#x3C;Callout></code> shortcode renders the same callout. <code>type</code> accepts <code>note</code>,\n<code>tip</code>, <code>info</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>danger</code>, <code>important</code>, or <code>caution</code>. Put the\nshortcode on its own lines.</p>\n<div class=\"admonition admonition-danger papers-callout papers-callout--danger\" role=\"note\" aria-label=\"Shortcode form\" data-callout=\"danger\"><p class=\"admonition-title papers-callout__title\">Shortcode form</p><div class=\"admonition-content\"><p>Never commit deployment credentials.</p></div></div>\n<h2>Code Inside Callouts And Tabs</h2>\n<p>Code blocks inside callouts and <code>&#x3C;Tabs></code> get the same copy button and syntax\ncolours as top-level blocks.</p>\n<div class=\"admonition admonition-tip\" role=\"note\" aria-label=\"Install command\"><p class=\"admonition-title\">Install command</p><div class=\"admonition-content\"><div class=\"papers-code\" data-code-language=\"bash\"><div class=\"papers-code__title\" data-code-title=\"\">install.sh</div><pre><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"papers-code__line\">npm install papers</span></code></pre></div></div></div>\n<h2>Synced Tabs</h2>\n<p>Give <code>&#x3C;Tabs></code> a <code>group</code> key to keep tab sets in sync. Markdown pages use the\nsame keys (<code>:::tabs pkg</code>), so a choice made on one page carries over to the\nother.</p>\n<div class=\"papers-tabs\" data-tabs-group=\"pkg\"><details class=\"papers-tabs__panel\" open><summary class=\"papers-tabs__label\">npm</summary><pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm run dev\n</code></pre></details><details class=\"papers-tabs__panel\" open><summary class=\"papers-tabs__label\">pnpm</summary><pre><code class=\"language-bash\">pnpm dev\n</code></pre></details></div>\n<h3>Nested Tabs</h3>\n<p>A <code>&#x3C;Tab></code> can hold another <code>&#x3C;Tabs></code> set:</p>\n<div class=\"papers-tabs\" data-tabs-group=\"os\"><details class=\"papers-tabs__panel\" open><summary class=\"papers-tabs__label\">macOS</summary><div class=\"papers-tabs\" data-tabs-group=\"pkg\"><details class=\"papers-tabs__panel\" open><summary class=\"papers-tabs__label\">npm</summary>Run <code>npm install papers</code>.</details><details class=\"papers-tabs__panel\" open><summary class=\"papers-tabs__label\">pnpm</summary>Run <code>pnpm add papers</code>.</details></div></details><details class=\"papers-tabs__panel\" open><summary class=\"papers-tabs__label\">Linux</summary>Install Node.js, then run <code>npm install papers</code>.</details></div>\n<h2>Steps And Cards</h2>\n<div class=\"papers-steps\"><ol>\n<li>Install the dependencies.</li>\n<li>Start the dev server.</li>\n</ol></div>\n<div class=\"papers-card-grid\"><div class=\"papers-card\"><p class=\"papers-card__title papers-card__title--link\"><a href=\"/docs/developer-guides/steps-and-cards\">Steps and cards</a></p><p>The Markdown syntax for steps and cards.</p></div><div class=\"papers-card\"><p class=\"papers-card__title papers-card__title--link\"><a href=\"/docs/developer-guides/callouts-and-code\">Callouts and code</a></p><p>Callouts and code blocks in Markdown.</p></div></div>\n<h2>GitHub Alerts</h2>\n<div class=\"admonition admonition-tip papers-callout papers-callout--tip\" role=\"note\" aria-label=\"Tip\" data-callout=\"tip\"><p class=\"admonition-title\">Tip</p><div class=\"admonition-content\"><p>GitHub alert syntax also works in MDX.</p></div></div>\n<h2>Code Fence Metadata</h2>\n<div class=\"papers-code\" data-code-language=\"bash\"><div class=\"papers-code__title\" data-code-title=\"\">setup.sh</div><pre><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"papers-code__line\">npm ci</span>\n<span class=\"papers-code__line papers-code__line--highlighted\">npm run generate:docs</span>\n<span class=\"papers-code__line\">npm run dev</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"papers-code\" data-code-language=\"diff\"><div class=\"papers-code__title\" data-code-title=\"\">package.json</div><pre><code class=\"language-diff\"><span class=\"papers-code__line papers-code__line--removed\" data-line-kind=\"removed\">-    \"build\": \"vite build\"</span>\n<span class=\"papers-code__line papers-code__line--added\" data-line-kind=\"added\">+    \"build\": \"npm run generate:docs &#x26;&#x26; vite build\"</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Code blocks in MDX pages use the same viewer as Markdown pages, with a copy button\nand syntax colours.</p>",
  "contentFormat": "html",
